[thin] Specified cup-floor section: Derek selected the 2.38 mm vertical casing while retaining the existing 2 mm floors, pocket heights and passage datums. The floor is the stack's 2.0 mm floor section above its 0.15 mm seat clearance, which leaves 2.05 mm under the B-fill pockets. The horizontal water-in and soda traverses keep 2.10 mm of backing beneath their bores.
alternatives: A 3 mm floor raises the traverses and pockets a millimetre in a 14.65 mm cup, which moves where their R14 bends cross into the lid, or makes the cup taller and moves the cap face.
