[thin] Outside the carbonator-sensing change: this ranked group is the existing cup casing and floor stock; its representative pair is 2.000 mm apart on the reservoir-side curve. The new straight reed passage is at native (0, 74) mm. The existing cup stock remains part of the separate cap layout review; this entry records its scope and establishes no printed strength or lifetime result.
alternatives: Thickening this local stock to 3 mm by moving its outside boundary changes the casing clearance; adding the stock inward consumes the adjacent cavity and requires reconciling its internal interfaces. Both belong to the cap layout review rather than the reed-position change.
